            <h1 class="detail-title">Scripture verification system</h1>
            <p class="detail-subtitle">A review-focused tool for Christian publishers who need accurate, auditable checking of Scripture references and quotations.</p>

            <div class="detail-body">
                <h3>The problem</h3>
                <p>Editorial teams still spend large amounts of time manually checking whether references exist, whether quotations match the stated translation, and whether deviations are acceptable or accidental.</p>
                <p>The work is essential, but it is slow, repetitive, and difficult to audit after the fact.</p>

                <h3>What the system does</h3>
                <p>The system processes a manuscript and produces a separate verification document designed for editorial review.</p>
                <ul>
                    <li>Confirms that references exist</li>
                    <li>Compares quoted text against the ESV word-for-word</li>
                    <li>Detects likely use of other translations</li>
                    <li>Flags deviations with clear review signals</li>
                    <li>Produces side-by-side comparisons for editors</li>
                </ul>

                <h3>What it is and is not</h3>
                <ul>
                    <li>An editorial verification tool for Christian publishers</li>
                    <li>Designed for accuracy, traceability, and review</li>
                    <li>Not a theological decision engine</li>
                    <li>Not a replacement for human editors</li>
                </ul>

                <h3>Who it is for</h3>
                <ul>
                    <li>Christian publishing houses</li>
                    <li>Theological editors and proof-readers</li>
                    <li>Publishers handling mixed-translation manuscripts</li>
                </ul>

                <h3>Development status</h3>
                <p>The product is currently in development planning, with architecture and workflows defined and an initial customer use-case established.</p>
                <p class="detail-note">If your organisation wants to discuss using the system, contact quickler and mention Scripture verification.</p>
            </div>
